{
  // Type-checks what `tsconfig.json` cannot see. That config has
  // `rootDir: "src"`, so `pnpm typecheck` has never looked at `test/` at all —
  // and `tsconfig.eslint.json` widens the scope for the linter's parser without
  // anybody ever running `tsc` over it. The gap is not theoretical: the port
  // change in step 4b-5 surfaced instantly in the fakes under `src/**/*.test.ts`
  // and would have surfaced in NO file under `test/`.
  //
  // What this exists to catch, stated so the flag decision below can be judged
  // against it: CONTRACT DRIFT (a fake that no longer satisfies the port, a test
  // calling a method that was deleted) and dead imports.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "rootDir": ".",
    "noEmit": true,

    // The one flag relaxed for test scope, and the reason is purpose rather than
    // convenience. In `test/` this rule fires 291 times on one shape — `rows[0].id`
    // after a query — and what it warns about there ("the array may be empty") is
    // something a test reports by FAILING, loudly, on the very next line. In `src/`
    // the same warning is about a production crash, which is why it stays on
    // there. Keeping it on here would cost ~291 hand-edits to buy a check the
    // suite already performs, and would have kept the contract-drift check —
    // the one that catches real bugs — switched off for another slice.
    //
    // If a test ever needs the strict reading back, narrow it in that file
    // (`const row = rows.at(0); expect(row).toBeDefined();`) rather than flipping
    // this back on for everything.
    //
    // ⚠ HAZARD, MEASURED 2026-08-20 — and the reason `typecheck:test` chains the
    // strict pass instead of standing alone. Test files import `src/`, so those
    // modules are part of THIS program too and are therefore checked with the flag
    // OFF. Probed deliberately: an unguarded `rows[0].id` planted in
    // `PrismaTransitionEffectRepository` was caught by `tsc --noEmit` (strict, src
    // only) and NOT caught here. So this config can never be the only checker, and
    // the script makes that impossible rather than trusting a reader of this
    // comment: `typecheck:test` = strict pass THEN this one.
    "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": false
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts", "test/**/*.ts"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist"]
}
